That's bad news and what I deduced from your
first error report.

I'm afraid there's no workaround to integer parameters
other than to marginalize them out of the models.
And I doubt that'll be possible for Poisson missing
data "parameters".

We're still brainstorming on a clever way to add
discrete samplers, but we don't see how to make it
both easy to specify the models and efficient to
sample.   We're interested in exactly this case,
because Poisson-like missing data is the only scenario
we've dreamed up where you have unbounded integer
parameters.

I'm guessing you'll need the missing data somewhere
else in the model specification.  If not, we are
going to add random number generators soon in the
generated quantities block to generate simulations.

- Bob

