You can also specify -march=native in CXXFLAGS, but that won't make too much of a difference.

For large values of N and n2, the loop in your model{} block is going to take a while. For a model that can be estimated by Gibbs sampling, a Gibbs sampler can take less time than a HMC sampler per iteration, although hopefully Stan will require fewer iterations than would a Gibbs sampler to get a reasonable effective sample size. Maybe someone else can jump in, but I don't see anything in your code that could be sped up substantially.

Ben

