On Monday, October 8, 2012 2:13:58 PM UTC-4, Joe King wrote:
> Oh, I guess the u2[1] to u2[300] are the individual school effects and I just have to compute the variance of them ?
>
> But it's strange that there are only 100 unique schools.

The length of u2 is whatever n2 is. See Matt Hoffman's comments especially; I think that could make a big difference. If you want to store the standard deviation of u2, you can put sigma into the transformed parameters {} block instead of the model{} block like

transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_u2;
  sigma_u2 <- sqrt(1/tau_u2);
}

or define sigma_u2 in the parameters {} block and drop tau_u2.

Ben

