On Monday, October 8, 2012 2:41:50 PM UTC-4, Joe King wrote:
> Thank you, although I am sorry that I don't understand. With the code you wrote below, u2 is then undefined and it doesn't parse.

Can't quite tell what you mean. It is always easier if you just attach the file that does or doesn't parse. Here is what I would do, approximately incorporating Matt and Bob's advice (also attached):

data {
    int<lower=1> n2 ;
    int<lower=1> N ;
    real y[N] ;
    int school[N] ;
}
parameters {

    real u2_z[n2] ;
    real<lower=0> sigma ;
    real<lower=0> sigma_u2;
    real <lower=0,upper=1000> beta;
}
model {
    real mu[N];
    for (i in 1:N)
      mu[i] <- beta + u2_z[school[i]] * sigma_u2;

    y ~ normal(mu,sigma);
    u2_z ~ normal(0, 1) ;

    // or some other prior on sigma and sigma_u2
    sigma ~ gamma(0.001000,0.001000) ;
    sigma_u2 ~ gamma(0.001000,0.001000) ;
}

Ben

