I'm guessing that sigma and sigma_u2 are close to zero? That may mean that there is not much point in having a multilevel model, or it may mean Stan is having a hard time sampling, or it may mean something else. I would try bounding sigma and sigma_u2 away from zero with something like
parameters {
  real<lower = .1, upper = 100> sigma;
  real<lower = .1, upper = 100> sigma_u2;
  ...
}

and comment out the priors on sigma and sigma_u2 in the model{} block. Then run it again. If the posterior mass piles up near .1, then maybe the error variances are just small.

