There's also a Java implementation of the collapsed
sampler in my company's open-source (but not free)
software along with a tutorial on usage:

   http://alias-i.com/lingpipe/demos/tutorial/cluster/read-me.html

The downside is the non-standard, restrictive, open-source
license:

   http://alias-i.com/lingpipe/web/licensing.html

It's very very easy to implement the collapsed sampler.  I
have a full derivation of integrating out the continuous
parameters linked from here:

http://lingpipe-blog.com/2010/07/13/collapsed-gibbs-sampling-for-lda-bayesian-naive-bayes/

- Bob

