Sebastian Weber vas escriure el dia dj, 18 oct 2012:

> Just found a neat way to get posterior samples from stan to coda:
>
> posterior <- extract(se$stanFit, inc_warmup=FALSE) posterior_coda <-
> do.call(mcmc.list, alply(posterior, 2, mcmc) )
>
> S <- ggs(posterior_coda)
>
>
> … but this version does not exclude element 4 in the third dimension
> which I did not understand. Of course, you need plyr loaded.

Thank you Sebastian,

Excluding element 4 is trivial:
posterior_coda <- do.call(mcmc.list, alply(posterior[,,-4], 2, mcmc) )

But of course your solution is much cleaner.

I have updated the post:
http://blog.xavier-fim.net/2012/10/processing-stan-samples-with-ggmcmc-2/

Best,

--
-  Xavier  -

