for (i in 1:N) {

  mu[i] <- beta + u2_z[school[i]] * sigma_u2 + gamma + v2_z[year[i]] * sigma_v2 ;
}

it parses and compiles. You will then run into a problem where your year variable is a factor rather than a numeric variable. Then it seems to run slowly, but maybe that is to be expected with an N of 30000.

Ben

