I'm having a problem compiling Stan 1.0.3 after modifying a source file (~/stan-src-1.0.3/src/stan/gm/command.hpp). After invoking make bin/libstan.a and make bin/stanc, make replies that the targets are up to date, which is unexpected. Shouldn't make see that there is a file which has changed and then recompile that file? What am I doing wrong? Of course, I can run make clean-all, and then recompile everything, but that is too slow. Thanks in advance for any ideas you may have.

